#: includes/help.php
msgid "Help & Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "This plugin adds a redirect field to posts and pages. Fill in a new address and every visit to that content is sent there. Leave the field empty and the content is displayed normally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "How to use"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Open the post or page in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Find the \"Simple Kit Redirect\" box in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Type the destination address and choose the redirect type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Save or update the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Accepted addresses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Absolute addresses, including other domains: https://example.com/new-page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Paths starting with a slash, resolved against this site address: /new-page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Protocol-relative addresses: //example.com/new-page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Anything else (javascript:, data:, mailto:, ftp:) is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Redirect types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "302 - Temporary: the default. Browsers do not keep it for long, so the destination can be changed later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "301 - Permanent: browsers and search engines may cache it for a long time. Visitors may keep going to the old destination even after the field is cleared."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Who still sees the original content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Previews, REST requests, feeds, robots.txt, sitemaps and 404 requests are never redirected. Password-protected content also keeps showing its password form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Logged-in editors are redirected like any visitor. To open the original content, add ?simplekitredirect=0 to the address. This only works for users who can edit the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Query strings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "When the destination has no query string, the query string of the original request is appended by default. Use the simplekitredirect_preserve_query filter to disable this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Developer filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "changes which post types can be redirected. Default: post and page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "decides at request time whether the redirect should happen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "enables or disables query string preservation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "changes the final destination before it is validated and sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Nothing happens: confirm the field was saved, the target is a full http(s) address or a path starting with a slash, and the destination is not the same address as the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Headers already sent: another plugin or the theme printed output before WordPress could send the redirect. Test with other plugins disabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "A 301 keeps redirecting after removal: the browser cached it. Clear the browser cache or test in a private window, and prefer 302 while testing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Page cache: purge the cache after changing a redirect."
msgstr ""

